00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,020
I thought of that quote today. Fear is the mind killer. I was thinking about it today, but I messed it up. I was thinking doubt makes fear. So I've messed up the phrase, but I want to be similar to that phrase.

2
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:36,880
But I kept on thinking that the reason people have fear is because you doubt something. So if you have no doubt, like if I know I can jump into that water and I'll be absolutely harmless, like it'll be fun, only fun, then I don't have to be scared of it.

3
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:47,900
And if people say they're not scared of something like a bungee jump, but they don't want to do it, it's because something tells them it's dangerous and there's a chance that they can be injured.

4
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:55,900
So it's always the doubt because I think about these things a lot and I realize that it's always doubt that makes the fear.

5
00:00:56,900 --> 00:01:04,620
I like the phrase knowledge dispels fear because the more knowledge you have, the less doubt you have and the less fear you have.

